      "content": "It's reassuring to hear that you're feeling normal right now, but it’s still wise not to dismiss the symptoms. While it's possible that because the symptoms have resolved so quickly, this could indeed be a benign episode like an aura that doesn't cause any real concern, we can't completely rule out other possibilities or permanent changes without professional evaluation, especially since these experiences are unusual for you.\n\nIf the symptoms had been accompanied by severe pain, vision loss, weakness or numbness, difficulty speaking, or any other concerning signs, it would have been important to go to the ER immediately. But in your case, since you're feeling back to normal, you should still consider tracking the occurrence: if it happens again, or if you notice any new symptoms, it would be prudent to seek medical advice. This way you're not ignoring a possible health issue, and you avoid the wait times at the ER just in case you need it. In general, it's better to be safe and have a healthcare professional assess any new and concerning symptoms.",
